=== Generated loot ===
{{LootChestItem|iron-helmet,level-enchanted-iron-helmet,level-enchanted-iron-chestplate,iron-leggings,level-enchanted-iron-leggings,iron-boots,level-enchanted-iron-boots}}

=== Natural generation ===
{{exclusive|java|section=1}}
Two [[armor stand]]s are found in each taiga [[village]] outdoor armory, one equipped with an [[iron helmet]], the other with an [[iron chestplate]].

=== Bartering ===
[[Piglins]] have about a 1.7% chance to [[barter]] [[iron boots]] enchanted with a random level of [[Soul Speed]] when given a [[gold ingot]].

=== Mob loot ===
[[Zombie]]s, [[skeleton]]s, and their variants have a chance to spawn with armor, with a 1.10% chance of it being iron armor. If killed by a [[player]], there is an 8.5% chance of dropping the armor. The dropped armor has a random durability and retains any enchantments it has.

{{IN|bedrock}}, [[pillager]]s and [[vindicator]]s that spawn in [[raid]]s have a small chance to drop an [[iron helmet]], [[iron chestplate]], [[iron leggings]], or [[iron boots]], in a badly damaged state, with a possibility of having a random enchantment.

=== Trading ===
{{main|Trading}}
Iron armor can be bought from [[armorer]]s.
{{trade sources|Iron Helmet|Iron Chestplate|Iron Leggings|Iron Boots}}

== Usage==
{{main|Armor#Usage}}
Wearing iron armor reduces damage taken from [[Armor#Damage types|most damage types]].

